ernment  I mean that's really stunning did I read  that footnote that you said that the the  Secret Service and the Confederates had  something like 800 some thousand dollars  to do you do a project in the North yeah  I think that's probably right it's a lot  of money back then yeah yeah but again  as I'm going to duck this one that's I  mean I know this from other sources it  is a lot of money but let's look at this  in context we do know that Jefferson  Davis at another point and this you know  when when Sherman was ravaging the South  a type of warfare that robert e lee  explicitly rejected attacking you know  attacking innocents and cities and  indeed populating whole state cities  Jefferson Davis turned down a proposal  by his own men to send smallpox infested  blankets into the north so I don't think  that the south is willing to go that far  what's your next book my next book is  going to be as different and it's kind  of bold and the sweeping as this book  but on a very different subject rather  than write a you know in one hand I'd  love to write about the Civil War again  because I have a whole body of knowledge  and it would make my life a lot easier  and certainly my wife's life and my  family life but I want to be challenged  I want to write something different and  if I feel excited and enthused about it  I'm convinced I can make readers equally  enthused it'll probably be about the  world of the 1780s to 1790s our guest is  Jay Winik here is the book 1885 the  month that saved America thank you very  much
 

